  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 3.3. An ArchiMate view of the health goal 'Establish Trusted Personal Health Records'. The goal and its four sub-goals (universally accessible verifiable records, consent-based sharing, trust and privacy, interoperability) sit at the top, with four outcomes beneath them. Below, a grey 'TPHR Implementation' grouping holds the capabilities (for example Health Record Management, Identity & Authentication, Consent Management, Trust Verification), the application services that realise them, and the application components (Lifelong Health Record, Client Registry, Consent Management Platform, PKI, SIEM, Terminology Service and others) that realise those.",
